{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>They answered</b>: The Gaon [Saadia] said that they added nothing now beyond the first reply, except that the first time they speak before the king, in the manner of קום נא שבה (arise, pray sit), whereas now it is singular form, for יקום אבי is not found. The reason: because they were afraid to speak before him, and they said: we have no answer to give back except what we answered the king."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The phrase יקום אבי appears to be Ibn Ezra's (or the Gaon's) illustration of a singular verb form; the referent is obscure and may be textually uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:19:05.009509009Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}